@startuml role-session
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Role sessions within one run (FR-04 / FR-05)
caption Invoke selection separately for each role and pass; run cleanup closes both roles.

state Entry <<choice>>
state "Validate pass request\nActive task/run; role and assignment identity\nEffective role model + session policy" as Validate
state "Assemble explicit context\nTask/spec, project instructions + design, code\nChecks, unresolved findings + repair responses" as Context
state SessionChoice <<choice>>
state "Verify reusable session\nSame task, run and role; model matches\nPrevious invocation ended; no concurrent pass" as Reuse
state "Retire previous session for this role\nStop/fence executor; save messages + usage\nRevoke session reference" as Retire
state "Create fresh role session\nNew session ID; configured role model\nNo prior conversation history" as Fresh
state "Evaluate outbound role handoff\nExact context manifest and feedback scope\nSee output-handoff-policy.puml" as HandoffGate
state "Deliver bounded assignment + context\nRecord exact context manifest and feedback refs\nVerify adapter accepted handoff" as Supply
state "Session ready for this pass\nReturn role/session/assignment identity" as Ready <<success>>
state "Needs attention\nInvalid context/config, identity or session failure" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Scope blocker\nConfirmed necessary work outside task spec" as ScopeBlock <<blocked>>

state "Close every session in this run\nStop/fence both roles and partial launches\nBlock new assignments and late-result transitions" as StopAll
state "Persist session endings\nMessages, findings, work references + usage\nRecord unavailable capture explicitly" as RecordEnds
state "Revoke all run session references\nPreserve task evidence outside conversations" as Revoke
state "Sessions closed\nCaller may finish outcome and release slot" as Closed <<success>>
state "Cleanup incomplete\nKeep slot reserved; expose recovery action\nNo new assignments" as CleanupPending <<attention>>

[*] --> Entry
Entry --> Validate : [select_for_pass]
Entry --> StopAll : [end_run; any outcome]
Validate --> Context : request valid; budget and permissions allow
Validate --> Attention : invalid, unsupported or stopped run
Context --> SessionChoice : required artifacts available and current
Context --> Attention : missing, contradictory or oversized required context
SessionChoice --> Fresh : [first pass for this role in this run]
SessionChoice --> Reuse : [later pass; reuse_within_run]
SessionChoice --> Retire : [later pass; fresh_per_pass]
Reuse --> HandoffGate : identity/config match; prior invocation terminal
Reuse --> Attention : missing, mismatched or still-active session
Retire --> Fresh : old session stopped/fenced; ending recorded
Retire --> Attention : retirement unconfirmed / caller closes run
Fresh --> HandoffGate : creation confirmed; model verified under configured policy
Fresh --> Attention : launch/auth/model failure / caller closes partial sessions
HandoffGate --> Supply : exact handoff allowed by policy
HandoffGate --> ScopeBlock : necessary extra work confirmed
HandoffGate --> Attention : correction, clarification, check failure\nor uncertain effects / caller records finding
Supply --> Ready : assignment accepted; session/context event recorded
Supply --> Attention : delivery unconfirmed after bounded reconciliation
Ready --> [*] : return session_ready
Attention --> [*] : return attention; caller invokes end_run cleanup
ScopeBlock --> [*] : return scope_blocked; caller invokes FR-10 handoff
StopAll --> RecordEnds : all executors stopped/fenced
StopAll --> CleanupPending : any executor cannot be stopped/fenced
RecordEnds --> Revoke : endings and evidence references persisted
RecordEnds --> CleanupPending : persistence unconfirmed
Revoke --> Closed : references revoked; no reuse in a later run
Revoke --> CleanupPending : revocation unconfirmed
CleanupPending --> StopAll : bounded recovery or explicit recovery action
Closed --> [*] : return sessions_closed

note right of SessionChoice
  Read only the requested role's independent setting.
  All four implementer/reviewer policy combinations work.
  Every NEW run starts with no reusable sessions,
  including human-feedback and prerequisite pickups.
  Preflight-only closure creates no coding sessions.
end note
note right of Supply
  Both roles receive the same task/spec identity.
  Reviewer context includes actual immutable changes,
  design and validation, not only an implementer summary.
  Fresh repair sessions receive stable finding IDs,
  current work and responses without another role's history.
  Reused sessions also receive current explicit context.
end note
note bottom of Ready
  The caller executes and records the pass before another assignment.
  A check failure or review finding starts a new pass through this selector.
  Retrying delivery of one assignment does not create a second invocation.
  No silent model, access-mode or session-policy substitution on failure.
end note
note bottom of StopAll
  All run exits use cleanup: completion, review wait, dependency block,
  clarification, cancellation and failure. Zero-session cleanup is valid.
  Run stop/cancellation during selection also enters StopAll.
  Logical fencing must prevent further effects before a slot is released.
end note
@enduml
